<title>GERMANY: Hesse Dec CPI up 0.3 pct, up 1.4 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Hesse Dec CPI up 0.3 pct, up 1.4 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The state statistics office in the German state of Hesse reported the following consumer price changes for December.</p>
<p>    Cost of living		December	    November</p>
<p>    Month/month (pct change)  +0.3		  unch</p>
<p>    Year/year		     +1.4		  +1.3</p>
<p>NOTE - This data is later combined with data from three other major German states to calculate the preliminary inflation figure for the whole of west Germany.  </p>
<p>The office gave the following breakdown of its December cost of living data:</p>
<p>						 Percentage change</p>
<p> Index/component			   mth/mth  yr/yr Index</p>
<p> Overall price index		     +0.3     +1.4  114.4</p>
<p> Prices excl. heating oil, fuel	+0.3     +1.1  114.2</p>
<p> Prices excl. seasonal goods	   +0.2     +1.4  114.9</p>
<p> Rents					 +0.2     +2.9  126.9</p>
<p> Household energy			  +0.3     +1.3  101.2</p>
<p> Personal goods, services and other  +2.4     +1.1  121.9</p>
<p> Transport and communications	  -0.2     +1.8  114.9</p>
<p> Furniture and other household goods unch     +0.6  111.1</p>
<p> Foodstuffs, drinks, tobacco	   +0.2     +0.6  109.3</p>
<p> Clothing, shoes			   unch     +0.7  108.5</p>
<p> Health and personal care items	+0.1     +1.0  111.3</p>
<p> Education, entertainment, leisure   +0.2     +0.8  111.5</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
